--[[
        UNIVERSAL CUSTOM ASSETS -- an animator for DOORS' things and your own

        Every setting, with its default. All optional, before the loadstring:

            _G.UniversalAssets = {
                Combo = { "U", "I", "O" },  -- hold Ctrl and type these: opens / closes the panel
                ComboTime = 2,              -- seconds allowed between those keys
                PlayKey = "P",              -- Ctrl + P: play / pause, also with the panel closed
                FreeCamKey = "F",           -- Ctrl + F: free camera on / off
                UIScale = 1.2,              -- size of the panel on a PC
                MobileScale = 0.8,          -- size of the panel on a phone
                MobileButtons = "auto",     -- the bar for phones: "auto", true (always) or false
                MoveSnap = 0.5,             -- studs   (0 = free)
                RotateSnap = 15,            -- degrees (0 = free)
                ScaleSnap = 0.05,           --         (0 = free)
                FreeCamSpeed = 24,          -- studs per second; Shift = a quarter
                LookSpeed = 0.25,           -- degrees per pixel, right mouse in the free camera
                OpenTime = 0.6,             -- seconds to open / close doors and drawers
                Folder = "UniversalAssets", -- where projects are saved
                SelfUrl = "...",            -- what Copy's loadstring loads (this script)
                Project = nil,              -- a project (what Copy puts here): loaded at start
                AutoPlay = false,           -- with Project: it plays as soon as it is loaded
            }
            loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bonellocristian78-lab/Gradish-Mode/main/UniversalAssets"))()

        THE PANEL (in Italian): four tabs, in the order you use them
            1 Aggiungi: DOORS' things, the Roblox toolbox, an ID
            2 Muovi: Studio's tools, place, duplicate, morph, undo / redo, free cam
            3 Anima: the easy way (1 "start here", 2 "arrive here in N s") and the keys
            4 Scena: save, load, your projects, copy as a loadstring, new scene
            Always under them: the timeline, Play / pause, Stop, loop, speed, the status.
            ? explains it all (it opens by itself until "Ho capito"). With the panel
            open, red dots in the world show the way the selected thing goes.

        THE EASY WAY
            Put the thing where it starts and press 1. Drag it where it arrives and press
            2: it gets there in the seconds written next to it. 2 again for more stretches.
            A model with a run / walk animation looks where it goes and runs (Auto).
            With the camera selected, 1 and 2 use the free camera.

        LIKE ROBLOX STUDIO
            Ctrl+1 select, Ctrl+2 move (arrows), Ctrl+3 scale, Ctrl+4 rotate (rings)
            Ctrl+Z undo, Ctrl+Y redo; click a model to select it
            hold the right mouse button to look around
            Free cam: WASD, E up, Q down, Shift slow, wheel forward, Z / X zoom, right mouse to look

        ON A PHONE
            A small bar at the top: UCA opens the panel, Play plays / pauses, Cam is the
            free camera (with its own arrows; drag a finger to look). Drag the panel by
            its title and the bar by ::. Place: tap where it goes. Tap a model to select
            it. The panel fits the screen and scrolls.

        THE TOOLBOX
            Type in the search box and press Cerca (or Enter): it searches Roblox's
            Creator Store, the Studio toolbox, for models. Seek, Rush, Ambush... are one
            tap away. "Solo animati" hides the models without animations. Tap a result
            to insert it: its scripts are taken out, its animations converted if needed.

        AUTO ANIM
            With Auto on, the selected model plays its own walk / run animation while
            its keys move it and its idle one while it stands (Seek runs between the
            keys you put down the hallway). Its keys' animations are then ignored.

        THE CAMERA
            "Telecamera" is first in the list of models: its keys are where the camera is and
            its zoom (set them from the free cam). On Play it flies through them, as in a
            DOORS cutscene. Play starts from the timeline's red line; Ctrl+P pauses.

        MORPH
            The selected model becomes your body: it follows you, you disappear, and it
            walks and stands with its own animations (the ones named walk / run / idle).

        COPY
            Copies a loadstring with the whole scene inside: pasted in the executor, it
            builds it again and plays it.

        KEYS
            Two keys = the model goes from one to the other in that time, with that
            easing (Smooth = a curve through all the keys). A key can also start an
            animation (kept going if the next key asks for the same one), a sound and
            an action: open / close (doors, drawers: anything on a hinge or a rail),
            lights off / on / flicker, hide / show.

        ANIMATIONS NOT OWNED BY THIS GAME
            Roblox plays an animation only in games owned by whoever uploaded it (in
            DOORS: LSPLASH). Any other one is converted on insert: its KeyframeSequence
            is downloaded and played by this script, joint by joint. Nothing is uploaded.
            Everything is local: only you see it.
]]

